<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>FAQ on KUMAKIKAI</title><link>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/</link><description>Recent content in FAQ on KUMAKIKAI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>FAQ (Smokeless)</title><link>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/smokeless/</link><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/smokeless/</guid><description>&lt;div id="basics" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3 id="what-kind-of-app-is-smokeless"&gt;What kind of app is Smokeless?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is an app for quickly recording &lt;code&gt;Smoked&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Avoided&lt;/code&gt; and reviewing counts and money values later. It can be used both as support for quitting smoking and as a simple log tool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3 id="what-does-avoided-record"&gt;What does &lt;code&gt;Avoided&lt;/code&gt; record?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It records a time when you wanted to smoke but did not. It does not automatically count smoke-free time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3 id="is-this-a-medical-app"&gt;Is this a medical app?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No. It does not provide medical treatment or medical services.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>FAQ (Uni:Note Pocket)</title><link>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/uni-note-pocket/</link><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/uni-note-pocket/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Uni:Note Pocket is an iPhone reader for backups created in Uni:Note.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id="basics" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-kind-of-app-is-uninote-pocket" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-use-uninote-pocket-by-itself" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="which-devices-are-supported" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="do-i-need-to-log-in-or-create-an-account" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3 id="help-1"&gt;Which devices and OS versions are supported?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requires an iPhone running iOS 17.0 or later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pocket is an iPhone reader requiring a backup created in Uni:Note on iPad. It cannot create a new note by itself. No separate app account is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create, edit, delete and reorder notes, pages, folders or question sets on iPad.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>FAQ (Uni:Note)</title><link>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/uni-note/</link><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kumakikai.github.io/en/faq/uni-note/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Uni:Note helps you organize handwritten notes and PDFs on iPad and review them using recordings, sticky markers and study tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id="basics" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-kind-of-app-is-uninote" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="which-devices-are-supported" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="which-languages-are-supported" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="is-apple-pencil-required" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="do-i-need-to-log-in-or-create-an-account" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3 id="help-1"&gt;Which devices and OS versions are supported?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requires an iPad running iPadOS 17.0 or later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handwriting uses iPad and Apple Pencil. Fingers scroll and manipulate attachments. No separate app account is required. Japanese, English, Korean, German, Traditional Chinese and French are supported.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id="notes-and-attachments"&gt;Notes and attachments&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div id="notes-and-pages" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="is-a-note-title-required" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-is-the-title-prompt-shown-when-i-first-open-a-new-subject" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-can-i-choose-when-i-create-a-subject" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-is-a-portrait-notebook" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-separate-notes-within-the-same-subject" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="how-are-new-pages-added" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-is-the-maximum-number-of-pages-in-a-note" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-delete-a-page" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-protect-a-note" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-edit-a-subject" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="can-i-organize-subjects-into-folders-on-home" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="what-can-be-restored-from-trash" class="guide-legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3 id="help-2"&gt;What if a note stops growing or cannot be found?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A note is limited to 150 pages. Create another note in the subject when needed. Leaving a new title blank uses the date. Search only covers entered note titles, not handwriting, page text, PDFs or subject names.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>